Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from the failure to release the connection tracking reference count (nfct) when socket buffers (SKBs) are either merged under NAPI's Generic Receive Offload (GRO) or reused. This leads to a situation where the reference count remains incremented, potentially causing memory leaks and incorrect connection tracking states when the SKBs are freed or reused.

